# intelligence/output/context/player_stats.json,
# intelligence/output/context/player_aliases.json, and
# intelligence/output/context/context_meta.json are INTENTIONALLY
# NOT ignored - these small files are what app.py loads at runtime
# via the Insight Engine, and Render only deploys what's committed
# to git. Everything else in output/ (the 22,000+ per-match event
# files, the full manifest, raw Cricsheet data) stays local-only -
# regenerate locally when you want fresh data, then re-commit the
# context files (including context_meta.json).
